<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<graphml xmlns="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns/1.0/graphml.xsd">
  <key id="d6" for="edge" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d5" for="edge" attr.name="keywords" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d4" for="edge" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d3" for="edge" attr.name="weight" attr.type="double" />
  <key id="d2" for="node" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d1" for="node" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d0" for="node" attr.name="entity_type" attr.type="string" />
  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;EUROPEAN SCIENTIFIC COMMUNITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The European Scientific Community was abuzz with groundbreaking discoveries and innovations during the early 19th century, providing a backdrop for the work of Gabriel Dépéret."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0086</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ACADEMY OF SCIENCES OF TURIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Founded in 1757, the Academy of Sciences of Turin was a prestigious institution dedicated to the pursuit of scientific knowledge, attracting brilliant minds and serving as a testament to Gabriel Dépéret's achievements."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0086</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALESSANDRO VOLTA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Alessandro Volta, an inventor of the electric battery, was a member of the Academy of Sciences of Turin, highlighting the institution's dedication to innovation and scientific excellence."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0086</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEMORIE DELLA REALE ACCADEMIA DELLE SCIENZE DI TORINO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PUBLICATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The academy's journal, featuring articles authored by Dépéret, showcases his research on topics such as geology and paleontology, demonstrating the academy's recognition of his contributions."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0086</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REAL ACADEMIA NACIONAL DE MEDICINA DE ESPAÑA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Real Academia Nacional de Medicina de España is a heritage institution dedicated to the advancement of medical sciences, where Dépéret was a member and contributed to various medical topics."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0086</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNIVERSITY OF PARIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dépéret pursued his higher education in medicine at the University of Paris, earning his degree in 1805 and being influenced by prominent medical scholars."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0086</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANTOINE LAVOISIER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Antoine Lavoisier, a prominent medical scholar, influenced Dépéret during his time at the University of Paris."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0086</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PIERRE-SIMON LAPLACE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pierre-Simon Laplace, another prominent medical scholar, influenced Dépéret during his time at the University of Paris."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0086</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DE LA PROPAGATION DES MALADIES ÉPIDÉMIQUES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PUBLICATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dépéret's treatise on the propagation of epidemic diseases, published in 1815, was widely acclaimed by the medical community and contributed to his recognition as a leading authority in the field of medicine."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0086</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GABRIEL DÉPÉRET&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gabriel Dépéret is a person who has made significant contributions to the field of medicine, particularly in disease prevention and control."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gabriel Dépéret was a French author and medical scholar who made significant contributions to the fields of science and medicine in the early 19th century, particularly in the areas of natural history, geology, paleontology, and epidemiology."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0086</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TURIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Turin is the city where the Academy of Sciences of Turin is located, and where Gabriel Dépéret found himself as a member of the prestigious institution."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0086</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1823 LETTER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A letter dated 1823, penned by the academy's secretary, formally invites Dépéret to join the institution, praising his outstanding work in the field of natural history."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0086</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1815 TREATISE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PUBLICATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dépéret's treatise on the propagation of epidemic diseases, published in 1815, was widely acclaimed by the medical community and contributed to his recognition as a leading authority in the field of medicine."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0086</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1820 MEMBERSHIP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dépéret's formal invitation to join the Real Academia Nacional de Medicina de España in 1820 marked a significant milestone in his career."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0086</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1805 DEGREE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dépéret earned his degree in medicine from the University of Paris in 1805, marking a significant milestone in his academic career."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0086</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1823 INVITATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The formal invitation to join the Academy of Sciences of Turin in 1823 was a testament to Dépéret's significant contributions to the field of natural history."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0086</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1815 RECOGNITION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dépéret's treatise on the propagation of epidemic diseases, published in 1815, was widely recognized by the medical community, contributing to his status as a leading authority."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0086</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1820 CONTRIBUTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dépéret's contributions to the Real Academia Nacional de Medicina de España in 1820 included studies on the treatment of tropical diseases and the development of vaccines."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0086</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LEGACY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Legacy is an organization that Gabriel Dépéret has contributed to, though the specific context is not provided, it is implied to be a medical institution or research organization."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0086</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FIELD OF MEDICINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Field of Medicine refers to the broader domain of medical research and practice where Gabriel Dépéret has worked."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0086</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DISEASE PREVENTION AND CONTROL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Disease Prevention and Control is a specific area within the field of medicine where Gabriel Dépéret's work has had a significant impact."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0086</data>
    </node>
